<title>RUSSIA: Russian chamber to debate anti-NATO resolution.</title>
<headline>Russian chamber to debate anti-NATO resolution.</headline>
<byline>Oleg Shchedrov</byline>
<dateline>MOSCOW 1997-03-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Russian deputies gave President Boris Yeltsin an extra reason to be tough with U.S. President Bill Clinton later this week by voting on Wednesday to debate a resolution declaring that Moscow would never join NATO.</p>
<p>In a separate move, the State Duma lower house, dominated by the communist opposition, also decided to ask Prime Minister Viktor Chernomyrdin to explain a radical government shake-up</p>
